   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = - x^{2} + 3 x + 3 \\) and \\( g(x) = x + 3 \\). Let R be the region bounded by the graphs of f and g. Find the exact volume of the solid generated when R is revolved about the line \\( y = 7 \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Multiply",
         [
            "Rational",
            104,
            15
         ],
         "Pi"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The graphs meet where \\( f(x) - g(x) = - x^{2} + 2 x = 0 \\), at \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). The axis lies above R, so g is farther from it: the outer radius is \\( R = 7 - g(x) = 4 - x \\) and the inner radius is \\( r = 7 - f(x) = x^{2} - 3 x + 4 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99058",
         "rule_named": "washer radii"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The volume is \\( \\pi\\int_{0}^{2} \\left(R^{2} - r^{2}\\right)\\,dx \\), and \\( \\int_{0}^{2} \\left(R^{2} - r^{2}\\right)\\,dx = \\frac{104}{15} \\), so the volume is \\( \\frac{104 \\pi}{15} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Rational",
               104,
               15
            ],
            "Pi"
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "washer method"
      }
